## Code Review (GPT-5.5)
Request changes 🔴 because CSS Modules demo exports lost the global theme variables that the revamped demo CSS now depends on.

### 1. Bugs / Issues

#### 1. 🔴 CSS Modules exports no longer include the demo color theme (blocking)

`docs/src/utils/createDemo.ts` now creates demos without the CSS Modules global theme:

```ts
export const createDemo = createDemoFactory({
  DemoContent,
});

export const createDemoWithVariants = createDemoWithVariantsFactory({
  DemoContent,
});
```

`docs/src/utils/demoExportOptions.ts` also only emits the minimal `demo.css` for CSS Modules variants:

```ts
const htmlHeadTemplate: ExportConfig['headTemplate'] = (props) => {
  const head = [htmlHeadWithDefaultStyles(props)];

  if (props.variantName === 'Tailwind') {
    head.push(htmlHeadWithTailwind(props));
  }

  return head.filter(Boolean).join('\n');
};

const transformVariant: ExportConfig['transformVariant'] = (variant, variantName, globals) => {
  globals = { ...globals };
  globals['demo.css'] = { source: demoCss };

  return { globals };
};
```

But the CSS Modules demos now rely heavily on theme tokens such as:

```css
.Accordion {
  border: 1px solid var(--color-neutral-950);
  color: var(--color-neutral-950);
}

.Trigger:hover:not([data-disabled]) {
  background-color: var(--color-neutral-100);
}
```

Those variables are defined for the docs site in `docs/src/css/index.css` via `@theme`, but they are not included in isolated CSS Modules exports. As a result, copied/exported CSS Modules demos in CodeSandbox/StackBlitz lose many colors, borders, backgrounds, and states because the referenced custom properties are undefined.

**Fix:** Keep exporting a CSS Modules theme file, update it to define the new `--color-neutral-*`, `--color-red-*`, `--color-blue-*`, and `--color-green-*` tokens, and continue linking/exposing it for `CssModules` variants; alternatively inline those variables into the generated `demo.css` for CSS Modules exports.

### 2. Accuracy and Completeness Assessment

I reviewed the full branch diff against freshly fetched `upstream/master`. The in-docs rendering path has the new tokens registered globally, so this issue is specifically with the exported/copied CSS Modules demo path rather than the main docs page styling.

### 3. Validation Coverage

I ran `git diff --check` and found no whitespace/conflict-marker issues. I did not run the full docs build or browser visual regression pass.
